flowchart TB
    accTitle: A topic per thing
    accDescr: A new thing, such as an alarm, a contribution or a release, opens a topic of its own in the chat, named after its repository and what it is. Its message with the buttons comes first, and its changes edit it there. Its drafts, the answer of Fix, the prompt of Edit, what Later brings back and the answers to what the maintainer asks in the topic follow in it; their question goes to the control repository together with the thing. Once the thing is done, its topic gets a check mark in front of its name and stays. When the maintainer deletes the topic, the next message of the thing opens a new one, with the thing's own message first. Without Threaded Mode, or when Telegram refuses the topic or a message in it, the thing goes on in the main view, as before. A refused topic pauses new topics for an hour, doubling up to four hours, and once the pause is over, the next change of an open thing moves it quietly into its own new topic.

    thing["A new thing: an alarm, a contribution, a release, code scanning"]
    open["`**createForumTopic** opens its topic, such as 🚨 demo needs you`"]
    first["`Its message with the buttons comes first; its changes edit it there`"]
    ask["`The maintainer asks in the topic: the text goes to the control repository **with the thing**`"]
    more["`Drafts, the answer of 🛠 Fix, ✏️ Edit, ⏰ Later and the answers follow in the topic`"]
    done["`**✅** in front of its name once it is done; the topic stays`"]
    gone["`The maintainer deletes the topic: the **next message** of the thing opens a new one, its own message first`"]
    main["`**Main view**, as before: no Threaded Mode, or a refused topic or message`"]

    thing --> open
    open --> first
    first -- "a question" --> ask
    ask -- "the answer" --> more
    first --> more
    more -- "merged, green again, ignored" --> done
    done -- "done for the maintainer" --> gone
    open -- "no topics, or Telegram refuses" --> main
    main -- "its next change, once Telegram opens topics again (after the pause)" --> open

    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef warn fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    class thing,ask you
    class open,first,more,gone bot
    class done done
    class main warn
